.TH "PERFORMANCERESOURCETIMING.CONTENTTYPE" "3JS" "April 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PerformanceResourceTiming.contentType \- PerformanceResourceTiming:
contentType property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]contentType\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]PerformanceResourceTiming\f[R] interface is a string indicating
the content type of the fetched resource, formatted as a MIME type and
subtype separated by a forward slash.
.PP
The content type is a minimized and \(lqstandardized\(rq version of the
MIME type that is extracted from the \f[CR]Content\-Type\f[R] HTTP
header sent in the resource\(cqs fetch response.
For JavaScript, JSON, SVG, and XML, the MIME type is replaced by a
representative MIME type/subtype string.
Other types supported by the browser are represented by the MIME
type/subtype string in the header (other information in the header is
discarded).
.SH VALUE
A string indicating the MIME type \(lqessence\(rq of the content.
This may be one of the following values:
.TP
\f[B]text/javascript\f[R]
JavaScript content.
.TP
\f[B]application/json\f[R]
JSON content.
.TP
\f[B]image/svg+xml\f[R]
SVG content.
.TP
\f[B]application/xml\f[R]
XML content (other than SVG).
.TP
MIME type/subtype
Any other MIME type/subtype supported by the user agent.
.TP
\f[B]\(dq\(dq\f[R] (empty string)
Returned for MIME types that are not supported by the browser, or if the
resource fetch failed due to CORS checks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Filtering resources
The \f[CR]contentType\f[R] property can be used to get specific resource
timing entries only; for example, only those related to scripts.
.PP
The following example uses a \f[CR]PerformanceObserver\f[R] to notify of
new \f[CR]resource\f[R] performance entries as they are recorded in the
browser\(cqs performance timeline.
The \f[CR]buffered\f[R] option is used for accessing entries from before
the observer creation.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] PerformanceObserver((list) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] javascriptResources = list
    .getEntries()
    .filter((entry) \f[B]=>\f[R] entry.contentType === \(dqtext/javascript\(dq);
  console.log(javascriptResources);
});

observer.observe({ type: \(dqresource\(dq, buffered: \f[B]true\f[R] });
.EE
.PP
The following example uses \f[CR]Performance.getEntriesByType()\f[R],
which only shows \f[CR]resource\f[R] performance entries present in the
browser\(cqs performance timeline at the time you call the method.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] scripts = performance
  .getEntriesByType(\(dqresource\(dq)
  .filter((entry) \f[B]=>\f[R] entry.contentType === \(dqtext/javascript\(dq);
console.log(scripts);
.EE
